      "content": "i get that, but \"balanced\" is way easier said than done. like, if you try to do both in a limited amount of time, aren't you just gonna end up watering down the hard parts? some people argue that if you don't prioritize the systemic injustice part, you're basically just teaching a fairy tale, and that's actually more harmful in the long run. don't you think an emphasis on those systemic issues is more necessary for a modern education?",
